// Windows resource script: gives cutpro.exe its own icon.
//
// The runtime QIcon that main.cpp installs only reaches windows the app has
// already opened - the titlebar and the taskbar button of a running process.
// Explorer, the Start menu, a pinned taskbar shortcut and the Alt+Tab entry all
// read the icon out of the executable's resource table instead, which is what
// this file writes. Without it those places fall back to the generic MinGW
// executable icon no matter what the running app looks like.
//
// The first icon in the table is the one Windows treats as the application icon,
// so IDI_ICON1 (id 1) is deliberate rather than incidental. The .ico it points at
// carries the 16/32/48/64/128/256 px sizes Windows picks between, generated from
// assets/image.png; the path is relative to this file.

IDI_ICON1 ICON "../assets/cutpro.ico"
